@@ -7,7 +7,21 @@ Delivers webhook payloads to subscriber endpoints.
 ```python
 from webhooks.dispatch import deliver
 
-deliver(subscriber_url, {"event": "created"})
+result = deliver(subscriber_url, {"event": "created"})
+result.delivered  # True if the last attempt got a 2xx response
+result.status  # last status code, or None if no response was received
+len(result.attempts)  # how many attempts were made
 ```
 
-A failed delivery is not retried.
+Only `http` and `https` URLs are accepted; anything else raises `ValueError`.
+
+## Timeouts and retries
+
+- Each request has a 5 second timeout (applied to connecting and to each socket read).
+- Connection errors, timeouts and 5xx responses are retried up to 3 times (so at most 4
+  attempts), sleeping 1s, 2s and 4s between attempts.
+- 4xx responses are final and are not retried.
+- Delivery blocks the calling thread for up to roughly 4 x 5s of requests plus 7s of backoff.
+- Every attempt is recorded in `result.attempts` as an `Attempt` with its number and either a
+  `status` or an `error` (the exception type name). Retries resend the same payload, so
+  subscribers should treat deliveries as at-least-once.
